# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #fields: two or more root occurrences of one head make a bare name ambiguous, never the
# first; Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-23 Q2: the literal heads count): D has two root heads y, y: 1 and y: 2, so the bare
# y of S is ambiguous. The admission fails when the program runs, before S runs: the implicit call throw, taken by
# catch: call. D\x keeps 1. Entry 7.
S:
    int: x 9
    int: y 2
end: S
D:
    int: x 1
    int: y 0
    y: 1
    y: 2
end: D
fn: run () int
    int: r 82
    call: S D
    catch: call ()
        r: 83
        if: D\x = 1
            r: 7
    ---
return: r
int: got run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
